## Intuition
To determine whether an ArrayList is sorted in non-decreasing order, we need to verify that every element is less than or equal to the element that follows it.

If at any point we find an element greater than the next one, the order is violated and the list is not sorted.

So the idea is simple: compare adjacent elements and check for any decreasing pair.

## Approach
1. Get the size of the ArrayList using nums.size().

2. Traverse the list from index 0 to n - 2.

3. For each index i, compare nums.get(i) with nums.get(i + 1).

4. If nums.get(i) is greater than nums.get(i + 1), return false immediately.

5. If the loop completes without finding any violation, return true.

6. This ensures we check all adjacent pairs in a single pass.

## Solution
```java[]
class Solution {
    public boolean isSorted(ArrayList<Integer> nums) {
        //your code goes here
        int n=nums.size();
        for(int i=0; i<n-1; i++){
            if(nums.get(i)>nums.get(i+1)) return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

## Complexity
**Time Complexity:** 
O(n)
We traverse the list once, comparing adjacent elements. In the worst case (already sorted list), all elements are checked.

**Space Complexity:**
O(1)
